.nh
.TH toolbox-rm 1
.SH "نام (NAME)"
toolbox-rm \- Remove one or more Toolbx containers

.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBtoolbox rm\fP [\fI--all\fP | \fI-a\fP] [\fI--force\fP | \fI-f\fP] [\fICONTAINER\fP\&...]

.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Removes one or more Toolbx containers from the host. The container should
have been created using the \fBtoolbox create\fR command.

.PP
A Toolbx container is an OCI container. Therefore, \fBtoolbox rm\fR can be used
interchangeably with \fBpodman rm\fR\&.

.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
The following options are understood:

.PP
\fB--all, -a\fP

.PP
Remove all Toolbx containers. It can be used in conjunction with \fB--force\fR as
well.

.PP
\fB--force, -f\fP

.PP
Force the removal of running and paused Toolbx containers.

.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.SS Remove a Toolbx container named \fBfedora-toolbox-gegl:36\fR
.EX
$ toolbox rm fedora-toolbox-gegl:36
.EE

.SS Remove all Toolbx containers, but not those that are running or paused
.EX
$ toolbox rm --all
.EE

.SS Remove all Toolbx containers, including ones that are running or paused
.EX
$ toolbox rm --all --force
.EE

.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\fBtoolbox(1)\fR, \fBpodman(1)\fR, \fBpodman-rm(1)\fR
